  "how_to_rebaseline": "A digest moving means behaviour moved. Name which cases moved and why, in the commit, before regenerating. If the reason is 'the generator changed', that is a data change and belongs in its own commit.",
  "note": "Golden blotters on the **irregular** generator -- variable session lengths with early closes, empty intervals, volatility clustering. The set in pre_context_refactor.json pins uniform=True and is the long-lived behaviour reference carried since Task 5; this one covers the path that actually found defects. Task 17 surfaced four of them here and none of them on the uniform path, so leaving the irregular path without a golden set left the more productive half unprotected.\n\nScore references re-baselined at pre-registration Amendment 3: sessions with no position now carry an idle-capital charge, so every score on every dataset moves. Blotter digests are unchanged and were asserted before regenerating -- the engine did not move, only the metric. superseded_*_amendment3 keeps the pre-charge values so the change is auditable rather than silent.",
